<Layout path="/about/">
  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="kicker">Material philosophy. Arifian composition.</p><h1>Subtle is<br />a considered whole.</h1><p class="lead">Arifian is Subtle’s author and curator. Soft Editorial Materialism brings together editorial composition, tonal Material principles, and interaction ideas from the wider design community.</p></div>
  <div class="wrap prose-layout"><div class="about-mark" aria-hidden="true">✳</div><div>
    <section><h2>Where the identity comes from</h2><p>Subtle combines editorial composition, tonal materiality, and rounded shape hierarchy. Its eight moods share one typography system, one component anatomy, and one interaction language.</p><p>Arifian's canonical design contract defines the colors, type families, shapes, modes, and motion vocabulary. The Tonal Hero, Soft Mosaic, Floating Inspector, Soft Command Bar, Context Capsule, Layered Sheet, Adaptive Header, and Media Surface are authored for Subtle.</p></section>
    <section id="provenance"><h2>Inspirations and credits</h2><p>Subtle is a synthesis of established ideas and authored choices. <a href="https://m3.material.io/">Material 3</a> informs tonal hierarchy, shape, and product ergonomics. <a href="https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/motion">Apple’s Human Interface Guidelines</a> inform motion and responsive feedback. <a href="https://tailark.com/">Tailark</a> informs open editorial rhythm.</p><p>Functionality research includes <a href="https://www.kibo-ui.com/">Kibo UI</a>, <a href="https://www.diceui.com/">Dice UI</a>, <a href="https://coss.com/ui">coss UI</a>, and <a href="https://kokonutui.com/">Kokonut UI</a>. Motion references include <a href="https://animate-ui.com/">Animate UI</a>, <a href="https://motion-primitives.com/">Motion Primitives</a>, <a href="https://reactbits.dev/">React Bits</a>, and <a href="https://magicui.design/">Magic UI</a>. The <a href="/motion/">motion reference page</a> records the brief’s wider reading list and its source post.</p><p>Jitendra Kumar’s <a href="https://medium.com/design-bootcamp/getting-your-border-radius-right-a-simple-trick-for-smooth-nested-containers-f6e0025e8c53">Getting Your Border Radius Right: A Simple Trick for Smooth Nested Containers</a> explains the <code>R_outer = R_inner + padding</code> heuristic: add the padding to the inner radius to align nested corners. The <a href="/foundations/#shape">Foundations demo</a> applies it to circular CSS corners with a uniform inset, counting borders and clamping the inner radius at zero. Deeper nesting and unequal insets need judgment.</p><p>Apple’s official SwiftUI documentation describes <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/roundedcornerstyle/continuous">continuous corners</a> as continuous-curvature corners and <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/concentricrectangle">ConcentricRectangle</a> as a shape that can resolve corner radii relative to a container. These are native SwiftUI APIs; this CSS circular-corner demo does not implement them.</p><h3>Behavior and owned source</h3><p><a href="https://base-ui.com/">Base UI</a> supplies accessible behavior for buttons, Select, tabs, dialogs, sheets, and toast notifications. The owned source approach follows <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/">shadcn/ui</a>. The component information architecture follows the family naming and ordering of the <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components">official shadcn component docs</a>; task categories and signature families extend that index. Presentation uses the Subtle semantic token contract throughout. <a href="https://recharts.github.io/">Recharts</a> renders the chart specimens. Inspiration links describe influence; dependency notices identify the code actually included.</p><p>The site uses <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, React, and TypeScript. The independent read-only API uses Elysia on Bun and the official Model Context Protocol TypeScript SDK.</p><p>The botanical media is an original vector study created for this site. Every person, project, metric, document, and conversation in the specimens is synthetic. The AI reply is prepared demo text.</p><p>Lexend Deca, Inclusive Sans, and JetBrains Mono are the specified font families. See the <a href="/licenses.txt">third-party license notices</a> for dependency and asset provenance.</p></section>
    <section id="agent-access"><h2>A public catalog for agents</h2><p>The read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) catalog is hosted on Arifian’s VPS. Connect an MCP-compatible agent to <code>https://subtle-api.arifian.web.id/mcp</code> using Streamable HTTP; the agent only receives published components, patterns, foundations, and mood tokens. Source and setup: <a href="https://github.com/arifian853/subtle.arifian.web.id">github.com/arifian853/subtle.arifian.web.id</a>.</p><pre><code>codex mcp add subtle --url https://subtle-api.arifian.web.id/mcp</code></pre><p>For local development, use the local endpoint after starting the API:</p><pre><code>codex mcp add subtle-local --url http://127.0.0.1:3001/mcp</code></pre><div class="tonal-card"><h3>Run locally</h3><p>Install <a href="https://bun.sh">Bun 1.4.2</a>, clone the repository, and install its workspace dependencies:</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/arifian853/subtle.arifian.web.id.git
cd subtle.arifian.web.id
bun install --frozen-lockfile</code></pre><p>Start the frontend and local MCP API in separate terminals:</p><pre><code>bun run dev
bun run dev:api</code></pre><p>The site opens at <code>http://localhost:4321</code>; the local MCP endpoint is <code>http://127.0.0.1:3001/mcp</code>. For an agent on another machine, use the VPS endpoint above instead. The local API binds to loopback only.</p></div><p>MCP tools: <code>list_catalog</code>, <code>search_catalog</code>, and <code>get_catalog_item</code>; resources use the <code>subtle://catalog/</code> scheme. Queries are limited to 80 characters, pages to 12 entries, and request bodies to 16 KB. The API has no mutation tools, arbitrary URL fetching, or file access.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Built to stay local</h2><p>Specimen state stays in your browser. Only the selected mood is persisted in local storage. The showcase includes no analytics, account flows, external fonts, or model integrations.</p></section>
  </div></div>
